WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.455
Is your property

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:02.320
yours?

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.247
Not if government takes it.

00:00:06.247 --> 00:00:07.080
And it can for

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.080
what it calls public use.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.440
Eminent domain law has long allowed

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.440
politicians to grab your property to

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.740
build roads,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:15.880
railroad tracks,

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.320
border walls.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.020
Which helps explain why

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.855
President Trump told Bret Baier,

00:00:20.855 --> 00:00:22.920
"I think eminent domain is wonderful."

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.520
I get it that a highway

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.780
or a border wall

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.280
is public use,

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.650
but 13 years ago the Supreme Court ruled

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.300
that New London, Connecticut

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.840
could bulldoze this little pink house

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.220
to make room

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.060
for a new business development.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.920
Eminent domain.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.040
They can take your home,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.096
they can take your land.

00:00:41.096 --> 00:00:42.935
In this soon-to-be released movie,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.340
Catherine Keener plays Susetto Kelo,

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.120
the owner of that little pink house,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.540
here learning that she has no right

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.700
to her own property.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.760
How could somebody break into my house

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.300
and take everything I have and go to jail?

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.820
Oh you could shoot him.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.020
I could shoot him!

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:01.560
I could kill them.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.061
But if they want the whole thing it's perfectly legal.

00:01:04.061 --> 00:01:05.703
The law does require the government

00:01:05.703 --> 00:01:08.420
to give you fair value for your property

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.700
But the bureaucrats decide

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:11.900
what fair value is.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.240
Mrs. Kelo! I have great news

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.320
They've agreed to increase their offer by $10,000.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.420
Susette Kelo didn't want the money.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.340
She wanted to keep her home,

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.820
but the government said no.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.160
So the bulldozers came.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.040
90 families left

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.980
Susette and six others refused to leave.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.240
While this was going on,

00:01:33.242 --> 00:01:35.339
I interviewed the real-life Kelo.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.907
We were backed into corners,

00:01:36.907 --> 00:01:38.250
like animals in a corner.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.920
I gave the city's lawyer a hard time about that.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.340
Any group of politicians can kick you out of your home.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.740
Well, that's true,

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.060
but that's true if you want to put up a road

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:47.920
for example,

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.020
the question is,

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.220
is this serving an important

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.060
public purpose

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.320
and we say it is.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.700
It's giving them a lot of power.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.060
Yes, that's true.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.380
A libertarian law firm,

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.844
The Institute for Justice took Susette's case

00:02:00.844 --> 00:02:03.360
all the way to the U.S. Supreme Court,

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.520
where Justice Sandra Day O'Connor

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.460
pushed back against the taking.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.360
Say you had a Motel 6

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:10.260
and the city says,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.760
well if we had a Ritz-Carlton

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.180
we would have higher taxes.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.280
Now is that okay?

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.160
Yes, Your Honor that would be okay.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.440
So you can take from A to give to B

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.080
if B pays more taxes?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.320
If it is a significant amount,

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.440
yes.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.380
Susette's lawyer responded this way:

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.614
The one thing that all poor neighborhoods share

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.300
is that they don't produce much tax revenue.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:34.760
If the court affirms the lower court's decision,

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.060
then you would put poor neighborhoods

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.800
and working-class neighborhoods like Fort Trumbull

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.720
in jeopardy.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:42.860
He was right.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.760
But the Supreme Court ruled

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.020
5-4 against Susette.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.840
U.S. Supreme Court today affirmed the power

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.516
of local governments to seize private property.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.240
The decision alarmed people

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.500
across America.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.100
Some states passed laws

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.321
limiting their politicians right to grab your property.

00:03:00.321 --> 00:03:01.141
In New London,

00:03:01.141 --> 00:03:02.940
people rallied around Susette.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:06.420
Hands off her home! Hands off her home!

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.480
Thank you all for fighting so hard.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.560
But that fight was over.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.800
They'd lost.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:12.420
Years later,

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.020
I went with Susette Kelo to

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.160
look at the place

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.671
New London said was going to be a

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.980
"booming development".

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.360
This was my stairs

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.020
and I had a long porch,

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.900
and this is where the house was.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.100
The city said they had to tear the houses down

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.960
because development would happen,

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.240
tax revenues

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.660
all kinds of cool new things

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.180
and yet,

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.080
this is what they got.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.520
No hotel or upscale housing,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.769
no conference center,

00:03:37.769 --> 00:03:39.080
no nothing.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.300
Kelo's house has been torn down

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.500
and the lot where it once stood is vacant.

00:03:43.504 --> 00:03:44.766
It's still empty.

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:45.840
Even today

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.760
13 years later, there's no development.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.240
It's just unused land.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.420
The politicians were wrong.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.640
This new movie is a good reminder

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.320
of just how powerful

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.400
and wrong

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.080
politicians often are.

